# B0: the BUILD-ONLY job of the window, run BEFORE A0 while production still serves. C2_ACTIONS=build opens no card, resets nothing and stops nothing: it makes the one image of
# the window (the thin tt-vllm layer over the P8 base, with request_width_warm and the generalised QWEN_FAST_M3_REQUEST_WARM) from the pushed tp4/warm4 commit.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH. The build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a is a PLACEHOLDER and the driver
# substitutes ONE new tag, never used before, in every template of this window after checking the tag is absent from the host's images (the build skips an image that already exists).
# Pass: the build log ends with the image tagged, the closure and provenance checks of the build pass. Stop rule: any failure stops the window before production is touched.
# Duration (estimate): 18-30 min, 90 at worst (the first build after a base change). Production serving is not downtime here.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/warm4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/warm4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or
# a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag, built by B0 from the pushed tp4/warm4 commit; the driver
# substitutes it in every template once the image is built. A later commit needs a new tag.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
